== Transportation ==

=== Rail ===

[[File:Okazaki Station.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Okazaki Station, serving both conventional rail and private rail services, connecting the prefecture to the national network.]]

Conventional rail services operated by [[Okaiken Railways]] connect the prefecture's cities and towns to the national network. [[Okaden]], a private railway based in Okazaki, is a private railway that provide local and express services to Central Okami.

=== Road ===
The prefecture is crossed by several national expressways, including the [[Okazaki Expressway]] which connects Okazaki to the national highway network.

=== Air ===
[[Okazaki Airport]] provides domestic service to major destinations within Okaiken.

== Education ==

[[File:Okazaki University.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Okazaki University, home to the prestigious Department of Martial Arts Studies.]]

Okazaki Prefecture maintains a comprehensive public education system operating under the authority of the prefectural board of education. The prefecture's unique educational approach integrates martial arts training into the standard curriculum at all levels.

Higher education institutions include [[Okazaki University]], which hosts the prestigious [[Department of Martial Arts Studies]], offering degrees in martial arts history, physical education, and sports science with emphasis on traditional disciplines. The [[Okazaki Martial Arts Academy]] provides specialized professional training for aspiring instructors and competitive athletes.

